// Old saves onto the ported quest - see scripts/general/scripts/port349.rs2.
//
// The old version of Eadgar's Ruse was re-created with an invented plan (dose the troll stew so
// Burntmeat hands over the key, distract the guard with a robe stuffed with a drunk parrot) on
// invented stages, and completed at 70:
//   0 not started, 10 started, 20 met Eadgar, 30 potion made, 40 stew dosed, 50 has the storeroom
//   key, 60 has the goutweed, 70 complete.
// The original (PlagueCityRS 349, OSRS varp values) completes at 110 and gets there a different way:
// Eadgar, Burntmeat, a drunk parrot hidden under the prison rack, a scarecrow of logs, 5 raw
// chickens, 10 grain and a dirty robe, a troll truth potion, the fake man for Burntmeat, the key in
// the kitchen drawers, and the goutweed out from under the storeroom guards.
//
// Mapping (the only places the two plans meet are "Burntmeat has given up the storeroom" and "I
// have the goutweed"; everything in between goes back to the last point both versions share):
//   0        -> 0    untouched
//   10       -> 10   ^eadgar_started: Sanfew has asked for goutweed - same meaning in both.
//   20,30,40 -> 15   ^eadgar_spoken_eadgar_first: the player has met Eadgar, but none of the old
//                    middle (thistle potion, dosed stew) is a step of the original. Eadgar sends
//                    them to the troll cook and the original plan runs from there. Leftover old
//                    items (troll potion, robe, drunk parrot, alco-chunks) stay where they are;
//                    the original takes each of them again when its step comes, and nothing
//                    hands out a second robe or parrot while one is owned. The one exception is
//                    the old fake man: the original's Eadgar builds the fake man himself at 86
//                    whether or not one is owned, so an old one would become a second. It is
//                    removed (inventory and bank) - it is a quest-only object with no other use.
//   50       -> 90   ^eadgar_got_burnt_meat: Burntmeat has given up the storeroom key; the player
//                    is holding it (the original's door takes it at this stage), and if it has
//                    been lost the kitchen drawers hand out another at this stage only.
//   60       -> 100  ^eadgar_unlocked_storeroom: the player has been in the storeroom and has the
//                    goutweed - Sanfew completes the quest on it at this stage (and the crate
//                    gives another if it has gone).
//   70+      -> 110  ^eadgar_complete: quest points, the Trollheim teleport gate and Sanfew's
//                    post-quest goutweed exchange all test >= / = ^eadgar_complete. Nothing the
//                    original checks afterwards lives outside %eadgar_quest, and the herblore xp
//                    is given only by [queue,eadgar_quest_complete], which is not re-run.
//
// %eadgar_scarecrow_items (bits 1-3 of %eadgar_bits) was the old version's "guard distracted" flag.
// In the original those bits are ^eadgar_given_logs (1) and ^eadgar_given_clothes (2), so an old
// flag of 1 would read as "logs already handed to Eadgar". Nothing reads the varbit any more, so it
// is cleared. %eadgar_grain and %eadgar_chickens were never written by the old version (and were
// not saved), so they are already 0.
[proc,port349_migrate_eadgar]
if (%port349_eadgar = ^true) {
    return;
}
def_int $old = %eadgar_quest;
if ($old > 0) {
    if ($old >= 70) {
        %eadgar_quest = ^eadgar_complete;
    } else if ($old >= 60) {
        %eadgar_quest = ^eadgar_unlocked_storeroom;
    } else if ($old >= 50) {
        %eadgar_quest = ^eadgar_got_burnt_meat;
    } else if ($old >= 20) {
        %eadgar_quest = ^eadgar_spoken_eadgar_first;
        if (inv_total(inv, eadgar_fake_man) > 0) {
            inv_del(inv, eadgar_fake_man, inv_total(inv, eadgar_fake_man));
        }
        if (inv_total(bank, eadgar_fake_man) > 0) {
            inv_del(bank, eadgar_fake_man, inv_total(bank, eadgar_fake_man));
        }
    } else {
        %eadgar_quest = ^eadgar_started;
    }
    %eadgar_scarecrow_items = 0;
    %eadgar_grain = 0;
    %eadgar_chickens = 0;
}
%port349_eadgar = ^true;
